    "source_semantic_class": "other_normative_clinical_instruction",
    "title_or_context": "Easy-to-read food labels can help you find foods low in sodium. This will help you keep track of the number of grams (g) or milligrams (mg) you consume each day. According to Food and Drug Administration regulations, no manufacturer can say that their product is “low-sodium” unless they can prove that claim. Learning to read food labels is a good first step in a sensible eating plan."
  },
